comments[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-03T11:08:43.782Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check 2026-08-03: searched all statuses for Codex session JSONL model probe, cross harness model resolver adapters, OpenCode Pi Cursor Aider Gemini model provenance, native harness metadata model version effort, and Codex model version automatic identity. Closed pm-ffz0a9 delivered a Claude-specific bounded resolver; closed pm-03pq3o delivered the generic identity shape; open pm-1wiugq measures inert coverage. No active item owns the non-Claude adapter fleet."
  "2026-08-03T20:38:40.632Z","harness:claude-code","Live confirmation on this repository 2026-08-03, read from the raw history entry of a Claude Code mutation made with no identity flags and no environment override.\n\nThe recorded provenance is now: author harness:claude-code with author_source detected, agent_harness claude-code, agent_model claude-opus-5 with agent_model_source probe, model source probe, effort xhigh from environment, version 2.1.220 from probe, and a stable agent_instance.\n\nThree of the five dimensions the mandate asks for are therefore live and automatic for this harness: harness, model, and reasoning effort. Against the long-standing baseline of model null on every one of tens of thousands of entries, that is the dimension crossing from never-observed to observed, and it did so through the non-environment resolver rather than through more environment keys, which is the design decision this item generalizes.\n\nThe two dimensions still missing on the same entry are exactly the two this item and its siblings own. role records the string 1, which is a boolean environment flag rendered as a value. topic is null. Neither is a regression and neither is fixed by another Claude-side key, which is why the adapter contract and the semantic inference layer remain the right shape for the remaining work.\n\nThe concrete consequence for this item is that the Claude adapter now has a working reference implementation for the model and version dimensions, so the other six built-in adapters have a template and a fixture shape to conform to rather than a specification alone.\n"
  "2026-08-04T09:18:05.477Z","harness:codex","Fresh Codex evidence 2026-08-04 with no PM_AUTHOR or --author: the plan mutation history records author=harness:codex, author_source=detected, agent_harness=codex, and a stable agent_instance, so zero-flag harness detection works. The same raw event has no agent_model, effort, role, or topic fields, so model/version/thinking-level and semantic session attribution remain incomplete for Codex. The external-package fleet smoke script also explicitly sets PM_AUTHOR=external-package-smoke and passes --author during init, masking whether package workflows honor automatic identity. Remove that test crutch only as part of this canonical cross-harness contract, with fixtures that prove all dimensions."
  "2026-08-14T14:40:21.731Z","harness:codex","Fresh Codex Desktop evidence 2026-08-14 with no PM_AUTHOR or identity flags: mutation pm-zzylb9 records author=harness:codex, author_source=detected, harness=codex, stable instance, inferred role=implementer, and inferred topic=pm-a8zm. Model and effort remain explicitly null, so the canonical adapter requirement is narrower than the 2026-08-04 snapshot but still open: resolve the actual Codex model family/version and reasoning level when the platform exposes them, otherwise persist an observable unavailable source instead of a silent null."
body: ""
